{"results":[{"record_id":"june_update_2026-06-10__rec_000194","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"Primary model paper introducing Bio-BLIP, a multimodal Q-former architecture. It explicitly fuses DNA, genes, proteins, and text, with a master Q-former that takes a natural-language instruction and generates structured variant captions.","evidence_snippet":"\"integrates four data modalities - DNA, genes, proteins, and text\"; \"fuses the Stage 1 modality-specific tokens with a natural-language instruction\"; \"produce a structured JSON caption for the variant\"; \"image-grounded text generation (ITG) loss\"; \"generative variant annotation\"; \"structured JSON objects for each single nucleotide variant\"; \"textual variant captions\"; \"the Master Qformer model attached to a frozen LLM\"; \"cross-attend to the layer-normalised Stage 1 visual tokens\"; \"Stage 2 training loss is next-token-prediction\"; \"The supervision signal is NTP loss on the answer tokens only\"; \"The LLM is not trained or fine-tuned\"; \"The total Stage 1 loss aggregates all three objectives\"; \"modality-specific Q-formers\"; \"input embeddings\"; \"human genetic variant annotation\"; \"variant annotation results\"; \"produces rich, transparent reasoning traces\"; \"Given a variant ID and/or biological embeddings, the model must produce a structured JSON caption\"; \"Textual variant captions\"; \"natural-language instruction\"; \"queries the input for the most task-relevant information\"; \"conditions a language model to generate outputs from these embeddings via SFT\"; \"The master Q-former model is a 6-layer InstructBLIP-style Q-Former\"; \"shared textual captions\"; \"The model must produce a structured JSON caption for the variant\"; \"variant annotation\"; \"generate outputs from these embeddings\"; \"text captions\"; \"